Commands: Delays in clock/4 (15 MHz)
DELAY  := 1101DDDD 0DDDDDDD 0DDDDDDD 0DDDDDDD  25 bit delay
OUTPUT := 1100DDDD 0DDDDDDD 0DDDDDDV 0VVVVVVV  8 bit output, 17 bit delay
ADC    := 10SSSXXX 0XXXXXXX 0XXYYYYY 0YYYYYYY
RESET  := 11110000 00000000 00000000 00000000  


Responses: Delays in clock (60 MHz)
CAPTURE := 110DDDDD 0DDDDDDD 0DDDDVVV 0VVVVVVV 0VVVVVVV 0VVVVVVV
STATUS  := 1010____
ERROR   := 1011XXXX
               0000 - OVERFLOW
               0001 - UNDERFLOW




16 bit alternatives (not implemented)
DELAY  := 1DDDDDDD 0DDDDDDD   14 bit delay
OUTPUT := 1______V 0VVVVVVV   8 bit output value
ADC   :=  1SSSS 0XXXXXXX

Variable size commands
OUTPUT2 := 11SSSSVV                       2 bit output (4 bit selector)
DELAY8  := 101DDDDD                       5 bit delay

OUTPUT8 := 1001XSSV 0VVVVVVV              8 bit output (2 bit selector)
DELAY16 := 1000DDDD 0DDDDDDD              12 bit delay
ADC     := 101000SS 0SSVVVVV 0VVVVVVV     12 bit ADC value with 4 bit selector

32 bit outputs and 16 12-bit adcs can be set with 4x OUTPUT8 and 16x ADC = 4x2
   +16x3 = 56 bytes, so at 20 MB/s can sustain 350k sets per second.
  
